<title>AUSTRALIA: Full table-Australian budget economic forecasts.</title>
<headline>Full table-Australian budget economic forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Treasury published these economic forecasts as the basis for its budget for the year to June 1998.</p>
<p>All figures are percentage change on previous year unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p>				OUTCOMES(b) ESTIMATES     FORECASTS</p>
<p>				  Year-av   Year-av   Year-av    4 qtrs</p>
<p>				  1995/96   1996/97   1997/98  to Jun98</p>
<p>INTERNATIONAL OUTLOOK Major trading partners</p>
<p>    Real GDP		     4.6	4.5	 4.5</p>
<p>    Inflation		    3.1	2.75	3</p>
<p>Crude oil (US$/barrel)	17.9     20.5	18.5</p>
<p>TWI index (c)		   54.8     59	  60</p>
<p>DEMAND AND OUTPUT (d) Private Consumption	    4.2	2.75	3.5	 3.75</p>
<p>Private Investment   Dwellings		    -12.9     -2	  11	  12</p>
<p>Total business		10.9     16	   8	   8</p>
<p>    non-dwelling const	23.8     19	  18	  21</p>
<p>    equipment		    6.2     15	   4	   2</p>
<p>Private final demand	   3.6	4.25	4.75	5</p>
<p>Public final demand	    0.9	2.25	2.25     -3</p>
<p>Total final demand	     3.0	3.75	4.25     0.25</p>
<p>  Farm and public authority  0.2	0	   0	   0</p>
<p>Gross National Expenditure   3.1	3.75	4.25	3.5</p>
<p>Exports			   10.8	7	   7	   8</p>
<p>Imports			    5.4	9	   9	   7</p>
<p>  Net exports (e)		1.1     -0.5     -0.25	 0</p>
<p>Gross Domestic Product (a)   4.1	3.25     3.75	 3.75</p>
<p>  Non-farm product	     3.5	3	  4	    4</p>
<p>  Farm product		  24.0	9	 -2	   -3</p>
<p>OTHER SELECTED ECONOMIC MEASURES Prices and Wages</p>
<p>    Consumer price index     4.2	1.25     1	    1.75</p>
<p>    Underlying		   3.2	2	  2	    2</p>
<p>    Gross non-farm deflator  2.8	2.25     2	    1.5</p>
<p>    Average earnings (f)     4.2	4.75     4	    4</p>
<p>Non-farm nominal unit  </p>
<p>    Terms of trade	     4.1	3.5	1.5	  1</p>
<p>Current account balance</p>
<p>    A$ billion		 -20.1    -20	-21</p>
<p>    pct of GDP		  -4.1     -3.75    -4</p>
<p>NOTES: (a) percentage change on preceding year unless otherwise indicated</p>
<p>(b) Calculated using annual original data</p>
<p>(c) Based on the technical assumption that the TWI remains around the average level reached in recent months.</p>
<p>(d) average 1989/90 prices  </p>
<p>(e) percentage point contribution to growth in GDP (a)</p>
<p>(f) average earnings (national accounts basis). Forecast earnings growth excluding the expected impact of above average Commonwealth Government redundancies is 4.5 percent in 1996/97 and four percent in 1997/98. The nominal unit labour cost estimate for 1996/97 is simarly affected</p>
<p>(g) the estimate in the final column represents the forecast level in the June quarter 1998</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
